---@field type? intercom.ArticleListType The type of the object - `list`.
---@field pages? intercom.CursorPages|distilled.Null
---@field total_count? number A count of the total number of articles.
---@field data? intercom.ArticleListDataList An array of Article objects

---An array of Article objects
---@alias intercom.ArticleListDataList intercom.ArticleListItem[]

---The data returned about your articles when you list them.
---@class intercom.ArticleListItem
---@field type? intercom.ArticleListItemType The type of object - `article`.
---@field id? string The unique identifier for the article which is given by Intercom.
---@field workspace_id? string The id of the workspace which the article belongs to.
---@field title? string The title of the article. For multilingual articles, this will be the title of the default language's content.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null The description of the article. For multilingual articles, this will be the description of the default language's content.
---@field body? string|distilled.Null The body of the article in HTML. For multilingual articles, this will be the body of the default language's content.
---@field body_markdown? string|distilled.Null The body of the article in markdown. For multilingual articles, this will be the body of the default language's content.
---@field author_id? number The id of the author of the article. For multilingual articles, this will be the id of the author of the default language's content. Must be a teammate on the help center's workspace.
---@field state? intercom.ArticleListItemState Whether the article is `published` or is a `draft`. For multilingual articles, this will be the state of the default language's content.
---@field created_at? number The time when the article was created. For multilingual articles, this will be the timestamp of creation of the default language's content in seconds.
---@field updated_at? number The time when the article was last updated. For multilingual articles, this will be the timestamp of last update of the default language's content in seconds.
---@field has_unpublished_changes? boolean Whether the published article has unpublished changes staged as a draft on top of its live content. For multilingual articles this reflects the default language's content; a pure draft (never published) reports `false`.
---@field draft_updated_at? number|distilled.Null The time, in seconds, when the staged draft was last edited, or `null` when there is no staged draft.
---@field url? string|distilled.Null The URL of the article. For multilingual articles, this will be the URL of the default language's content.
---@field parent_ids? intercom.ArticleListItemParentIdsList The ids of the article's parent collections or sections. An article without this field stands alone.
---@field ai_chatbot_availability? boolean Whether the article is available for AI Chatbot. For multilingual articles, this will be the value of the default language's content.
---@field ai_copilot_availability? boolean Whether the article is available for AI Copilot. For multilingual articles, this will be the value of the default language's content.
---@field ai_sales_agent_availability? boolean Whether the article is available for AI Sales Agent. For multilingual articles, this will be the value of the default language's content.
---@field created_by_id? number|distilled.Null The ID of the teammate who created the article. For multilingual articles, this will be the creator of the default language's content.
---@field updated_by_id? number|distilled.Null The ID of the teammate who last updated the article. For multilingual articles, this will be the last editor of the default language's content.
---@field exclude_from_article_suggestions? boolean Whether the article is excluded from Fin AI Agent article suggestions.
---@field help_center_audience? intercom.ArticleListItemHelpCenterAudience|distilled.Null The audience that can view this article in the Help Center. `everyone` means all users and visitors can view it; `restricted` indicates a custom audience ruleset. For multilingual articles, this is the article-level audience.
---@field scheduled_publish_at? number|distilled.Null The Unix timestamp (in seconds) at which the article is scheduled to be published. `null` when no publish is scheduled. Mutually exclusive with `scheduled_unpublish_at` — at most one pending schedule exists per article.
---@field scheduled_unpublish_at? number|distilled.Null The Unix timestamp (in seconds) at which the article is scheduled to be unpublished. `null` when no unpublish is scheduled. Mutually exclusive with `scheduled_publish_at` — at most one pending schedule exists per article.
---@field default_locale? string The default locale of the help center. This field is only returned for multilingual help centers.
---@field translated_content? intercom.ArticleTranslatedContent|distilled.Null
---@field tags? intercom.Tags

---The audience that can view this article in the Help Center. `everyone` means all users and visitors can view it; `restricted` indicates a custom audience ruleset. For multilingual articles, this is the article-level audience.
---@alias intercom.ArticleListItemHelpCenterAudience "everyone"|"all_users"|"all_visitors"|"all_leads"|"all_visitors_and_leads"|"restricted"

