---Conversations are how you can communicate with users in Intercom. They are created when a contact replies to an outbound message, or when one admin directly sends a message to a single contact.
---@class intercom.Conversation
---@field type? string Always conversation.
---@field id? string The id representing the conversation.
---@field title? string|distilled.Null The title given to the conversation.
---@field created_at? number The time the conversation was created.
---@field updated_at? number The last time the conversation was updated.
---@field waiting_since? number|distilled.Null The last time a Contact responded to an Admin. In other words, the time a customer started waiting for a response. Set to null if last reply is from an Admin.
---@field snoozed_until? number|distilled.Null If set this is the time in the future when this conversation will be marked as open. i.e. it will be in a snoozed state until this time. i.e. it will be in a snoozed state until this time.
---@field open? boolean Indicates whether a conversation is open (true) or closed (false).
---@field state? intercom.ConversationState Can be set to "open", "closed" or "snoozed".
---@field read? boolean Indicates whether a conversation has been read.
---@field priority? intercom.ConversationPriority The priority level of the conversation. Returns one of none, low, medium, high, or urgent.
---@field admin_assignee_id? number The id of the admin assigned to the conversation. If it's not assigned to an admin it will return 0.
---@field team_assignee_id? number The id of the team assigned to the conversation. If it's not assigned to a team it will return 0.
---@field company? intercom.Company|distilled.Null The company associated with the conversation.
---@field tags? intercom.Tags
---@field conversation_rating? intercom.ConversationRating|distilled.Null
---@field source? intercom.ConversationSource
---@field contacts? intercom.ConversationContacts
---@field teammates? intercom.ConversationTeammates|distilled.Null
---@field custom_attributes? intercom.CustomAttributes
---@field first_contact_reply? intercom.ConversationFirstContactReply|distilled.Null
---@field sla_applied? intercom.SlaApplied|distilled.Null
---@field statistics? intercom.ConversationStatistics|distilled.Null
---@field conversation_parts? intercom.ConversationParts
---@field linked_objects? intercom.LinkedObjectList
---@field ai_agent_participated? boolean Indicates whether the AI Agent participated in the conversation.
---@field ai_agent? intercom.AiAgent|distilled.Null
---@field sales_agent_participated? boolean Indicates whether the Sales Agent participated in the conversation.
---@field sales_agent? intercom.SalesAgent|distilled.Null
---@field channel? intercom.ConversationChannel|distilled.Null The channel through which the conversation was initiated and its current channel.
---@field external_references? intercom.ConversationExternalReferencesList References linking this conversation to records in an external helpdesk or CRM system. Populated for Fin Standalone workspaces synced from an external platform; an empty array otherwise. Sorted alphabetically by `type` and capped at 20 entries.
---@field monitor_evaluations? intercom.ConversationMonitorEvaluationsList The latest QA monitor evaluation for each monitor that has evaluated this conversation, whatever its result. Only included when `include_monitors=true` is passed as a query parameter.
---@field scorecards? intercom.ConversationScorecardsList QA scorecard results for this conversation. Only included when `include_scorecards=true` is passed as a query parameter.

