---@field name? string Name of the attribute.
---@field full_name? string Full name of the attribute. Should match the name unless it's a nested attribute. We can split full_name on `.` to access nested user object values.
---@field label? string Readable name of the attribute (i.e. name you see in the UI)
---@field description? string Readable description of the attribute.
---@field data_type? intercom.DataAttributeDataType The data type of the attribute.
---@field options? intercom.DataAttributeOptionsList List of predefined options for attribute value.
---@field api_writable? boolean Can this attribute be updated through API
---@field messenger_writable? boolean Can this attribute be updated by the Messenger
---@field ui_writable? boolean Can this attribute be updated in the UI
---@field custom? boolean Set to true if this is a CDA
---@field archived? boolean Is this attribute archived. (Only applicable to CDAs)
---@field created_at? number The time the attribute was created as a UTC Unix timestamp
---@field updated_at? number The time the attribute was last updated as a UTC Unix timestamp
---@field admin_id? string Teammate who created the attribute. Only applicable to CDAs

